INSERT INTO `brand_prompts` VALUES (12,1,'Analyze the BOQ, identify every MCCB requirement, select the correct MCCB series / model / release from the provided price list, and add all mandatory and condition-based accessories. You MUST follow every rule below exactly.\n\n## 1. General MCCB selection rule — what to identify\nWhen an MCCB is mentioned in the BOQ, identify the following from the BOQ:\n- MCCB series / construction type (Single-Break or Double-Break)\n- MCCB model / frame\n- Number of poles\n- Current / rating\n- Icu\n- Ics\n- Release type\n- Protection requirement (LSI or LSIG)\n- Required accessories\n- Required indication\n- Required communication / metering functions\n\nThen select the corresponding item from the provided price list.\n\n## 2. Mandatory rules\n1. The BOQ is the source for determining the required MCCB specifications.\n2. The price list is the authoritative source for selecting the actual product, product code and price.\n3. Do not invent part numbers, model numbers, prices, product descriptions or accessories.\n4. Every selected MCCB and accessory MUST exist in the provided price list.\n5. All accessories must be compatible with the selected MCCB series, model, pole configuration and release type.\n6. Do not substitute one series, release type, protection type or accessory for another.\n7. If the exact item cannot be identified from the price list, report: \"Not found in price list – manual verification required\".\n8. If multiple price-list items are possible and the BOQ does not provide enough information to identify the correct one, report: \"Multiple possible price-list items – additional BOQ information required\".\n9. Do not make assumptions when required BOQ information is missing or unclear.\n\n## 3. Price-list validation\nThe provided price list is the authoritative source for: product code, model, series, description, rating, pole configuration, release, protection, accessory and price. Every MCCB and accessory selected MUST be validated against it.\n1. Do not create product codes.\n2. Do not assume product codes.\n3. Do not create prices.\n4. Do not assume prices.\n5. Do not select an accessory that is not available in the price list.\n6. Do not substitute an apparently similar product without confirming compatibility.\n7. Match the BOQ requirements against the price-list technical description.\n\nIf the exact item is not available: \"Not found in price list – manual verification required\".\nIf multiple items match and the BOQ does not contain enough information: \"Multiple possible price-list items – additional BOQ information required\".\n\n## 4. Critical rule — no assumptions\nThe BOQ and the price list must be treated as the authoritative inputs. Do NOT:\n- Guess a missing series.\n- Guess a missing model.\n- Guess a missing rating.\n- Guess a release type.\n- Convert LSI to LSIG.\n- Convert LSIG to LSI.\n- Upgrade or downgrade a release.\n- Substitute TM and MP.\n- Substitute iTRP1 and iTRP3.\n- Substitute iTRP3 with iTRP4 / iTRP5.\n- Assume 3P when 4P is required.\n- Assume 4P when 3P is required.\n- Select a different Spreader Link configuration.\n- Invent a price-list code.\n- Invent a price.\n- Add optional accessories that are not required by the BOQ.\n\nWhen information is insufficient, clearly flag the item for manual verification instead of making an assumption.\n\nThe ONE permitted default: when the BOQ does not state the breaker construction at all, treat it as Single-Break and select from the single-break products (see the series rule). Do not flag that as missing information.',1,'2026-10-02 11:15:22.780','2026-10-03 02:40:32.262','MCCB selection — general rules','file_016CTry4SuWm9jJojRv8GMYN','COMPLETED',NULL,'2026-10-03 02:40:32.261'),(13,1,'LK DSINE DN Series MCCBs are Single-Break MCCBs. The DN series has two release types:\n- TM — Thermal-Magnetic release\n- MP — Microprocessor-based release (MTX 1.0, MTX 2.0, MTX 3.0)\n\n## Choosing the MTX release from the BOQ protection\nWhen the BOQ requires a SINGLE-BREAK (DN) MCCB with a microprocessor release but names the protection rather than the MTX model:\n- BOQ protection LSI → MTX 1.0.\n- BOQ protection LSIG → MTX 2.0 (the base LSIG release). Select MTX 3.0 only when the BOQ names MTX 3.0 or requires its functions (communication, voltage / current modules, advanced protections).\n- In the price list the DN microprocessor rows are listed per release model (\"Microprocessor Release MTX1.0\" / \"MTX2.0\" / \"MTX3.0\") — select the row of the release decided here; never pick a different MTX model because it is cheaper.\n- This mapping applies ONLY to single-break breakers; a double-break breaker takes a DZ iTRP release (see the DZ rule).\n\n## MTX 1.0 — LSI protection\nMTX 1.0 provides L (overload), S (short-circuit) and I (instantaneous) protection.\n- If the BOQ specifies MTX 1.0, select the corresponding DN Series MCCB with MTX 1.0 release from the price list.\n- Include only L, S and I. Do not add Ground-Fault / Earth-Fault protection unless the BOQ specifies it separately.\n\n## MTX 2.0 — LSIG protection\nMTX 2.0 provides L, S, I and G (Ground-Fault / Earth-Fault) protection.\n\nGround-fault protection:\n- 4P MCCB: ground-fault protection is built-in.\n- 3P MCCB: an External Neutral CT AND an Adaptor Kit for External Neutral CT are required — include both whenever MTX 2.0 is selected for a 3P MCCB.\n\nAvailable modules: External Display and Metering Module; UN-CO Module; Power Supply Module; 2 m Cable for the External Display and Metering Module.\n\nModule rules:\n- BOQ requires External Display and Metering → include the External Display and Metering Module, the 2 m Cable and the Power Supply Module.\n- BOQ requires Modbus breaker status indication / control → include the UN-CO Module and the Power Supply Module.\n- BOQ requires both External Display and UN-CO → include only 1 × Power Supply Module and 1 × 2 m Cable. Never duplicate the Power Supply Module or the 2 m Cable.\n\n## MTX 3.0 — LSIG protection\nMTX 3.0 provides L, S, I and G protection.\n\nGround-fault protection:\n- 4P MCCB: built-in.\n- 3P MCCB: External Neutral CT and Adaptor Kit for External Neutral CT are required.\n\nAvailable modules: External Voltage Module; Current Module; Communication Module; UN-CO Module; Power Supply Module.\n\nPower supply rule: if ANY of the External Voltage, Current, Communication or UN-CO modules is required, the Power Supply Module MUST also be included — exactly 1 × Power Supply Module however many modules are selected. Never duplicate it.',1,'2026-10-02 11:15:22.780','2026-10-03 02:40:32.921','DN series (Single-Break) & MTX releases','file_01DiKxZFvzUm17c4MmFBUQPy','COMPLETED',NULL,'2026-10-03 02:40:32.920'),(14,1,'LK DSINE DZ Series MCCBs are available as Single-Break and Double-Break MCCBs. The BOQ describes the construction with words such as \"Single-Break\" or \"Double-Break\" — do NOT expect it to contain DZ1, DZ2, DZ4, DZ6 or DZ7 identifiers.\n\n## Construction → product category (applies to EVERY MCCB in the BOQ)\nFirst read the construction type the BOQ gives for the breaker, then pick only from the matching category of products in the price list:\n- BOQ says \"Single-Break\" (or single break / single breaker) → select from the SINGLE-BREAK MCCB products of the price list.\n- BOQ says \"Double-Break\" (or double break / double breaker) → select from the DOUBLE-BREAK MCCB products of the price list.\n- BOQ does NOT mention the construction at all (construction null on EVERY line, whatever the feeder role or rating) → treat the breaker as SINGLE-BREAK and select ONLY from the single-break products named in the series mapping below; a double-break series (DZ2 / DZ4 / DZ6 / DZ7) is NOT allowed for any breaker, incoming or outgoing, in that case. This default is the one permitted assumption: do not flag a missing construction type for confirmation, and do not pick a double-break product unless the BOQ asks for one.\n\n## Series mapping (LK)\n- Single-Break → DZ1 series (the DN series is also single-break: use DN when the BOQ names a DN / MTX release, or when the DZ1 range has no product at the required rating / poles / release)\n- Double-Break → DZ2 / DZ4 / DZ6 / DZ7\n\nSelection rules:\n- Single-Break → select the corresponding single-break MCCB (DZ1, or DN as above) from the price list.\n- Double-Break → determine the applicable series among DZ2, DZ4, DZ6 and DZ7 by matching the BOQ technical requirements (pole configuration, current rating, frame size, Icu, Ics, release type, other stated specifications) against the price list. Do NOT pick DZ2 / DZ4 / DZ6 / DZ7 on assumption alone.\n- Never interchange Single-Break and Double-Break.\n- A DZ frame this rule does not list (e.g. DZ0): classify its construction from the price-list / reference text for the DZ range before using it; never use it for a construction the reference text does not support.\n- The BOQ may give the construction per FEEDER ROLE (\"incoming shall be double-break, outgoing single-break\"): apply it line by line using each breaker\'s role — the incomer and the outgoings of the same panel then come from DIFFERENT series.\n- If the BOQ asks for Double-Break but does not give enough information to determine WHICH DZ series, report: \"Multiple possible price-list items – additional BOQ information required\".\n\n## Release classification\nDZ Series MCCBs come with TM (Thermal-Magnetic) or MP (Microprocessor-based) releases.\n- BOQ specifies TM → select the TM / Thermal-Magnetic release.\n- BOQ specifies MP → select the MP / Microprocessor-based release.\n- Match the release to the selected DZ series, MCCB model, pole configuration, rating and price-list item.\n- Never substitute TM for MP or MP for TM. If the release type is missing or unclear, flag it for confirmation.\n\n## Protection → release model (applies to DOUBLE-BREAK / DZ breakers only)\nThe construction decides the series first; the protection then decides the release model WITHIN that series. For a DZ breaker: LSI → iTRP1, LSIG → iTRP3 (iTRP4 / iTRP5 only when the BOQ names them). In the price list the DZ microprocessor rows are listed per release model (\"Microprocessor Release iTRP1\" / \"iTRP3\" / \"iTRP4 & iTRP5\") — select the row of the release decided here; never pick a different iTRP model because it is cheaper. A SINGLE-BREAK breaker with LSI / LSIG takes the DN series with the matching MTX release (see the DN rule), not a DZ iTRP breaker.\n\n## iTRP1 — LSI protection\niTRP1 provides L, S and I protection.\n- BOQ specifies LSI → select the corresponding DZ Series MCCB with iTRP1 release.\n- Include only L, S and I; do NOT include G / Ground-Fault protection.\n- Never substitute iTRP3, iTRP4 or iTRP5 for iTRP1. The LSI specification in the BOQ determines the release.\n\n## iTRP3 — LSIG protection\niTRP3 provides L, S, I and G protection.\n- BOQ specifies LSIG for a double-break (DZ) breaker → select the corresponding DZ Series MCCB with iTRP3 release. Never substitute iTRP1 for iTRP3.\n- Ground-fault protection: 4P MCCB → built-in; 3P MCCB → External Neutral CT and Adaptor Kit for External Neutral CT are required.\n- Modules: UN-CO Module and Power Supply Module. If the BOQ requires Modbus breaker status indication / control, include the UN-CO Module and one Power Supply Module.\n\nMandatory classification: always determine whether the BOQ specifies LSI or LSIG — LSI → iTRP1, LSIG → iTRP3. Never infer, interchange or upgrade the release. If the BOQ does not clearly specify LSI or LSIG, flag: \"Protection / release type not specified – manual confirmation required\".\n\n## iTRP4 and iTRP5 — LSIG protection\nBoth provide L, S, I and G protection. iTRP4 adds advanced current-based protection functions; iTRP5 adds advanced energy-based protection functions.\n- Select iTRP4 or iTRP5 ONLY when the BOQ specifically requires that release. Never replace iTRP3 with iTRP4 or iTRP5 automatically.\n- Ground-fault protection: 4P MCCB → built-in; 3P MCCB → External Neutral CT and Adaptor Kit for External Neutral CT are required.\n- Available modules: Communication Module; Auxiliary Power Supply Module; Temperature Module with Thermal Sensors; Zone Selective Interlocking (ZSI) Module; Programmable Relay Module.\n- Include the Communication, Temperature, ZSI and Programmable Relay modules ONLY when the BOQ requires them.\n- The Auxiliary Power Supply Module is mandatory for iTRP4 and iTRP5: always include 1 × Auxiliary Power Supply Module when either is selected.',1,'2026-10-02 11:15:22.780','2026-10-03 02:40:33.647','DZ series & iTRP releases','file_01GZuBMPyUbfTLAiciTBBRBh','COMPLETED',NULL,'2026-10-03 02:40:33.645'),(15,1,'Regardless of MCCB series, model, release type or protection type, EVERY MCCB gets these two accessories:\n\n## Extended Rotary Handle — 1 No.\nSelect the Extended Rotary Handle that matches the selected MCCB series / model / configuration from the price list. Never omit it and never assume a part number.\n\n## Spreader Link — matching the pole configuration\n- 3P MCCB → 3P Spreader Link\n- 4P MCCB → 4P Spreader Link\n\nNever interchange 3P and 4P Spreader Links, never omit the Spreader Link, and verify the accessory code and price against the price list. If the MCCB pole configuration is missing or unclear, flag it for confirmation.',1,'2026-10-02 11:15:22.780','2026-10-03 02:40:34.248','Mandatory accessories (handle + spreader)','file_01GUEEzBpEKw5R4tpxHWdHZx','COMPLETED',NULL,'2026-10-03 02:40:34.247'),(16,1,'For these models ONLY — DN0-100D, DN0-125D and DZ0-125D — Ics is 50% of Icu.\n\nFormula: Ics = Icu × 50%. Example: Icu = 36 kA → Ics = 18 kA.\n\nApply this calculation only to the models listed above; do not apply it to other MCCB models unless the BOQ explicitly says so. If the BOQ already states Ics, validate it against this rule.',1,'2026-10-02 11:15:22.780','2026-10-03 02:40:34.853','Ics rule for DN0 / DZ0 frames','file_01VXX8rnY5wbUVbJDRAo5ucA','COMPLETED',NULL,'2026-10-03 02:40:34.852'),(17,1,'## Digital MFM / Ammeter\nIf the BOQ contains a Digital MFM, Multifunction Meter, Digital Ammeter or Ammeter, also include:\n- 6A, 1-Pole MCB — 1 No.\n- Neutral Link — 1 No.\n- Disconnecting Terminal Block — 3 Nos.\n- Current Transformer (CT) — 3 Nos.\n\nCT selection: choose the CT rating from the applicable feeder / MCCB current rating, and validate the CT product code and rating against the price list. Never invent a CT ratio.\n\n## Phase / RYB indication\nIf the BOQ mentions Phase Indication, RYB Indication or R-Y-B Indication, include:\n- Red Indication Lamp — 1 No.\n- Yellow Indication Lamp — 1 No.\n- Blue Indication Lamp — 1 No.\n- 6A, 1-Pole MCB — 3 Nos.\n- Neutral Link — 1 No.\n\nValidate each component against the price list.\n\n## MCCB ON / OFF / TRIP indication\nDetermine the exact indication requirement from the BOQ:\n- ON / OFF / TRIP → Red, Green and Amber Indication Lamps (1 No. each), 6A 1-Pole MCB (1 No.), Neutral Link (1 No.), MCCB Auxiliary Contact, Trip Alarm Contact.\n- ON / OFF only → MCCB Auxiliary Contact. Do NOT include a Trip Alarm Contact unless TRIP indication is also required.\n- TRIP only → Trip Alarm Contact. Do NOT include an MCCB Auxiliary Contact unless ON/OFF indication is also required.',1,'2026-10-02 11:15:22.780','2026-10-03 02:40:35.476','Metering & indication accessories','file_01FpqtHM9Q4rfdPNr4usyRjb','COMPLETED',NULL,'2026-10-03 02:40:35.474'),(18,1,'## Duplicate accessory rule\nBefore adding any accessory, check whether the same accessory has already been selected for the same MCCB. Do NOT duplicate accessories unnecessarily.\n\nExamples:\n- MTX 2.0 with both External Display and UN-CO required → include only 1 × Power Supply Module and 1 × 2 m Cable.\n- MTX 3.0 with several modules that each need a Power Supply Module → include only 1 × Power Supply Module.\n\nGeneral rule: for each MCCB, consolidate all accessory requirements before generating the final output. If the same accessory is required by several functions, combine the requirement into one quantity unless the price-list specification explicitly requires multiple units.\n\n## MCCB selection priority — follow this sequence for every MCCB\n1. Identify the MCCB construction: Single-Break or Double-Break, using the exact wording / meaning from the BOQ; when the BOQ does not mention it, use Single-Break.\n2. Identify the series: map the construction to the applicable DZ / DN series according to the brand rules.\n3. Identify the pole configuration: 3P or 4P.\n4. Identify the rating: current rating, frame / model, Icu, Ics.\n5. Identify the release exactly as the BOQ states it: TM, MP, MTX 1.0, MTX 2.0, MTX 3.0, iTRP1, iTRP3, iTRP4 or iTRP5. Do NOT infer a release that is not specified.\n6. Identify the protection: LSI or LSIG, and match it to the applicable release.\n7. Apply the ground-fault rules when LSIG is selected: 4P → built-in ground-fault; 3P → External Neutral CT + Adaptor Kit.\n8. Identify the required modules: add only the modules the BOQ specifically requires, and apply the mandatory Power Supply rules.\n9. Add the mandatory accessories for every MCCB: Extended Rotary Handle and the correct Spreader Link.\n10. Add the condition-based accessories — check MFM / Ammeter, RYB indication, ON/OFF/TRIP indication, communication, metering, auxiliary contacts, trip alarm, CT, Neutral Link and any other explicitly required accessory.\n11. Remove duplicates: consolidate duplicate accessories and modules.\n12. Validate every selected MCCB and accessory against the price list.\n13. Final validation: only after all checks are completed may the final output be generated.\n\n## Final validation checklist — verify ALL of the following before finalising\n1. Correct MCCB construction selected.\n2. Correct MCCB series selected.\n3. Correct model / frame selected.\n4. Correct pole configuration selected.\n5. Correct current rating selected.\n6. Correct Icu selected.\n7. Correct Ics selected, or correctly calculated where applicable.\n8. Correct release type selected.\n9. L / S / I / G protection requirements satisfied.\n10. LSI / LSIG classification matches the BOQ.\n11. Ground-fault requirements checked for 3P / 4P.\n12. External Neutral CT added where required.\n13. Adaptor Kit for External Neutral CT added where required.\n14. Correct CT rating selected.\n15. Required modules added.\n16. Mandatory Power Supply Module added where applicable.\n17. Auxiliary Power Supply Module added for iTRP4 / iTRP5.\n18. Extended Rotary Handle added for EVERY MCCB.\n19. Correct 3P / 4P Spreader Link added for EVERY MCCB.\n20. MFM / Ammeter accessories added where applicable.\n21. RYB indication accessories added where applicable.\n22. ON/OFF/TRIP accessories added according to the exact BOQ requirement.\n23. Duplicate accessories removed.\n24. Every selected MCCB exists in the price list.\n25. Every selected accessory exists in the price list.\n26. No product code or price has been invented.\n27. Any uncertain selection is clearly flagged for manual verification.\n28. The final output contains both the MCCB selection and the complete accessory breakdown.',1,'2026-10-02 11:15:22.780','2026-10-03 02:40:36.005','Selection sequence & de-duplication','file_01LBdr67PrE34SL1qRU9He2v','COMPLETED',NULL,'2026-10-03 02:40:36.003'),(19,1,'Always answer in the exact structured format the system asks for (the JSON fields it specifies) — never replace it with tables or prose. Within that format:\n- Put a catalog number only when it is a confirmed price-list match; otherwise leave it null.\n- Start the \"reason\" / note field of each line with the selection status — one of these phrases — and then, after a dash, state in a few words WHICH BOQ fact and rule drove the selection (e.g. \"Selected – Price List Match – construction not stated → single-break per rule; LSIG → <release the rule maps to>\"). Never leave only the status phrase:\n  - \"Selected – Price List Match\"\n  - \"Not found in price list – manual verification required\"\n  - \"Multiple possible price-list items – additional BOQ information required\"\n  - \"BOQ information missing – manual confirmation required\"\n- For an accessory, state in the reason which MCCB it belongs to and why it is required (e.g. \"3P Spreader Link for the 250A 3P DZ4 incomer\").\n- Every MCCB must have its accessories listed as their own lines, so the output contains both the MCCB selection and the complete accessory breakdown.',1,'2026-10-02 11:15:22.780','2026-10-03 02:40:36.638','Output & status wording','file_01Y1V37b27FUzESPUS5fTCZw','COMPLETED',NULL,'2026-10-03 02:40:36.637');
