INSERT INTO `quote_messages` VALUES (30,15,'USER','Please prepare a quote from BOQ_dz.xlsx.','2026-10-03 05:12:02.922','[{\"name\":\"BOQ_dz.xlsx\",\"path\":\"D:\\\\cladue\\\\jobwork\\\\backend\\\\uploads\\\\jobwork\\\\1791004322862-4e1a66014974.xlsx\",\"mimeType\":\"application/vnd.openxmlformats-officedocument.spreadsheetml.sheet\"}]'),(31,15,'ASSISTANT','Here\'s your draft quote (LK). 15 of 35 line(s) priced from the brand files, 20 flagged for review.\n\nThe BOQ does not state breaker construction, so every MCCB is selected as single-break. Breakers of 250A and above use DN MTX2.0 (LSIG; 4P, so ground fault is built in), and breakers below 250A use thermal-magnetic DZ1 (36kA) or DN (25kA), each with an Extended Rotary Handle and a 4P Spreader. Items that could not be fixed from the price lists are flagged for manual verification with no code or price: the MCBs (curve not stated), MFM, earth fault relay and voltmeter selector have several possible codes, and the indication lamps, voltmeter, CTs, busbars, neutral links and terminal blocks are not found.\n\nApplied: rules LK · MCCB selection — general rules, LK · DN series (Single-Break) & MTX releases, LK · DZ series & iTRP releases, LK · Mandatory accessories (handle + spreader), LK · Ics rule for DN0 / DZ0 frames, LK · Metering & indication accessories, LK · Selection sequence & de-duplication, LK · Output & status wording; brand files trained into Claude.\n\nAsk me to adjust quantities, swap a part, or explain any line.','2026-10-03 05:14:30.540',NULL),(32,15,'USER','','2026-10-03 05:16:40.341','[{\"name\":\"BOQ_dz_Backup.xlsx\",\"path\":\"D:\\\\cladue\\\\jobwork\\\\backend\\\\uploads\\\\jobwork\\\\1791004600302-8c03f3de9965.xlsx\",\"mimeType\":\"application/vnd.openxmlformats-officedocument.spreadsheetml.sheet\"}]'),(33,15,'ASSISTANT','Regenerated the quote from BOQ_dz_Backup.xlsx (LK). 19 of 34 line(s) priced from the brand files, 15 flagged for review.\n\nBill of materials for the PTTA LT panels using LK products. Incomers are double-break: a DZ7 iTRP3 LSIG breaker (630A) on Panel 1 and a DZ4 iTRP3 breaker (250A) on Panels 2 & 3. Outgoings are single-break: DN2 MTX2.0 for 250A, and DZ1 thermal-magnetic for ratings below 250A, each with its extended rotary handle and 4P spreader terminals. Several items have no price-list match and are flagged for manual verification: indication lamp full codes, neutral links, terminal blocks, CTs, analog voltmeter, busbars, the MFM model choice and the earth fault relay.\n\nApplied: rules LK · MCCB selection — general rules, LK · DN series (Single-Break) & MTX releases, LK · DZ series & iTRP releases, LK · Mandatory accessories (handle + spreader), LK · Ics rule for DN0 / DZ0 frames, LK · Metering & indication accessories, LK · Selection sequence & de-duplication, LK · Output & status wording; brand files trained into Claude.\n\nAsk me to adjust quantities, swap a part, or explain any line.','2026-10-03 05:18:46.452',NULL),(34,16,'USER','Please prepare a quote from BOQ_dz.xlsx.','2026-10-03 05:35:15.020','[{\"name\":\"BOQ_dz.xlsx\",\"path\":\"D:\\\\cladue\\\\jobwork\\\\backend\\\\uploads\\\\jobwork\\\\1791005714971-2597560197dc.xlsx\",\"mimeType\":\"application/vnd.openxmlformats-officedocument.spreadsheetml.sheet\"}]'),(35,16,'ASSISTANT','Here\'s your draft quote (LK). 19 of 34 line(s) priced from the brand files, 15 flagged for review.\n\nBill of materials for Sub LT Panel 1 (1 no.) and Sub LT Panels 2 & 3 (2 nos.). The BOQ does not state breaker construction, so every MCCB is single-break. Breakers of 250A and above are DN with the MTX2.0 (LSIG) release; breakers below 250A are DZ1 thermal-magnetic, quoted at 36kA because DZ1 has no 25kA variant. Lines with a null catalogue number (LED indicators, neutral links, terminal blocks, metering CTs, voltmeters, busbars, earth-fault relay and CBCT) need manual pricing.\n\nApplied: rules LK · MCCB selection — general rules, LK · DN series (Single-Break) & MTX releases, LK · DZ series & iTRP releases, LK · Mandatory accessories (handle + spreader), LK · Ics rule for DN0 / DZ0 frames, LK · Metering & indication accessories, LK · Selection sequence & de-duplication, LK · Output & status wording; brand files trained into Claude.\n\nAsk me to adjust quantities, swap a part, or explain any line.','2026-10-03 05:37:03.438',NULL),(36,16,'USER','','2026-10-03 05:40:06.130','[{\"name\":\"BOQ_dz_double.xlsx\",\"path\":\"D:\\\\cladue\\\\jobwork\\\\backend\\\\uploads\\\\jobwork\\\\1791006006115-48d46db5093c.xlsx\",\"mimeType\":\"application/vnd.openxmlformats-officedocument.spreadsheetml.sheet\"}]'),(37,16,'ASSISTANT','Regenerated the quote from BOQ_dz_double.xlsx (LK). 21 of 35 line(s) priced from the brand files, 14 flagged for review.\n\nBOM for one Sub LT Panel 1 and two identical Sub LT Panels 2 & 3, built per the BOQ notes. Incomers are double-break: 630A DZ7 and 250A DZ4, both iTRP3 LSIG. Outgoings are single-break: 250A uses DN2 MTX2.0 LSIG, and breakers below 250A use DZ1 thermal-magnetic. Every MCCB carries an extended rotary handle and a 4P spreader set. Items with no confirmed price-list code are left without a catalogue number or price for manual verification: the Gen Next Pro lamps (exact colour/voltage code not printed), analog voltmeter, LT metering CTs, neutral links, disconnecting terminal blocks, earth-fault CBCT and busbars.\n\nApplied: rules LK · MCCB selection — general rules, LK · DN series (Single-Break) & MTX releases, LK · DZ series & iTRP releases, LK · Mandatory accessories (handle + spreader), LK · Ics rule for DN0 / DZ0 frames, LK · Metering & indication accessories, LK · Selection sequence & de-duplication, LK · Output & status wording; brand files trained into Claude.\n\nAsk me to adjust quantities, swap a part, or explain any line.','2026-10-03 05:42:09.066',NULL),(38,17,'USER','Please prepare a quote from MV panel-adv chemical stms.xlsx.','2026-10-03 05:44:54.109','[{\"name\":\"MV panel-adv chemical stms.xlsx\",\"path\":\"D:\\\\cladue\\\\jobwork\\\\backend\\\\uploads\\\\jobwork\\\\1791006294075-fc08d642bd17.xlsx\",\"mimeType\":\"application/vnd.openxmlformats-officedocument.spreadsheetml.sheet\"}]'),(39,18,'USER','Please prepare a quote from MV panel-adv chemical stms.xlsx.','2026-10-03 05:53:41.952','[{\"name\":\"MV panel-adv chemical stms.xlsx\",\"path\":\"D:\\\\cladue\\\\jobwork\\\\backend\\\\uploads\\\\jobwork\\\\1791006821904-1c4c6457a557.xlsx\",\"mimeType\":\"application/vnd.openxmlformats-officedocument.spreadsheetml.sheet\"}]'),(40,18,'ASSISTANT','Here\'s your draft quote (LK). 31 of 47 line(s) priced from the brand files, 16 flagged for review.\n\nBOM for two LK LT panels: MV Panel with an 800A 4P incomer and Sub MV Panel with a 400A 4P incomer. The BOQ asks for double-break breakers throughout, so the incomers are DZ7/DZ6 with the iTRP3 (LSIG) release and the outgoings are DZ2/DZ4/DZ7 thermal-magnetic; each breaker carries its extended rotary handle, spreader terminals and indication accessories. Some items are not in the attached LK price lists and are left without a catalogue number for manual verification: neutral links, metering CTs, terminal blocks, amber lamps, the Type 1 SPD, and the MFM / ELR variants. For 250A, 200A and 160A the smallest double-break frame was chosen, and the BOQ\'s \'fixed magnetic\' outgoing release should be confirmed against DZ\'s adjustable short-circuit setting.\n\nApplied: rules LK · MCCB selection — general rules, LK · DN series (Single-Break) & MTX releases, LK · DZ series & iTRP releases, LK · Mandatory accessories (handle + spreader), LK · Ics rule for DN0 / DZ0 frames, LK · Metering & indication accessories, LK · Selection sequence & de-duplication, LK · Output & status wording; brand files trained into Claude.\n\nAsk me to adjust quantities, swap a part, or explain any line.','2026-10-03 05:58:20.929',NULL);
